        "Time loses its promised reward",
        "After news of Lady Macbeth’s death, Macbeth speaks of repetitive time and life as a futile performance. His bleak outlook belongs to this character at this moment; it is not automatically Shakespeare’s final statement about all life. A messenger’s report that the wood seems to move then breaks the first apparent guarantee of safety."
